10. Code itself has rhyme

Now flip it.

Not numbers encoded in code.

Code can itself rhyme.

These functions:

def fahrenheit(c):
    return 1.8 * c + 32
def affine(x):
    return a * x + b
def normalize_then_shift(x):
    return scale * x + offset

are surface-different but structurally rhyme:

f(x)=ax+b

Their abstract syntax trees have nearly the same relational shape.

So code rhyme can be defined over an AST feature extractor:

\phi(\text{program})
=
\text{normalized syntax tree}

Then:

\operatorname{CodeRhyme}(P,Q)
=
\operatorname{similarity}
(
\phi(P),\phi(Q)
)

You can strip variable names:

x * 2 + 1
temperature * 2 + 1
score * 2 + 1

Surface semantics differ.

Computational meter is identical.

